{
  "info": {
    "name": "SG Backend — Sprint 2 Complete",
    "description": "Sprint 2: Phone-first OTP Auth, Refresh Tokens, Rate Limiting\n\nNew in this sprint:\n- POST /api/auth/send-otp    — generate & send 6-digit OTP via Sparrow SMS (Twilio fallback)\n- POST /api/auth/verify-otp  — verify OTP; creates account on first use, logs in on subsequent calls\n- POST /api/auth/resend-otp  — resend OTP (rate limited: 5/15min)\n- POST /api/auth/refresh     — rotate refresh token, issue new access+refresh tokens\n- POST /api/auth/logout      — revoke single device refresh token\n- POST /api/auth/logout-all  — revoke all sessions for authenticated user\n- PUT  /api/auth/device      — store/update FCM device token\n- Zod validation on all write endpoints (auth, ride, wallet, bid, paymentMethod schemas)\n- Helmet security headers on all responses\n- Redis-backed rate limiting: 5/15m send-otp, 10/15m verify-otp+login, 30/15m refresh, 300/m global\n- Access token TTL: 15m | Refresh token TTL: 30 days | Stolen token detection (revoke-all)\n\nDB migrations:\n  backend/migrations/sprint2_auth_tokens.up.sql   — run this first\n  backend/migrations/sprint2_auth_tokens.down.sql — rollback\n\nEnv vars added:\n  SPARROW_SMS_TOKEN      — Sparrow SMS API token\n  SPARROW_SMS_FROM       — sender ID (default: SG)\n  TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID     — Twilio account SID\n  TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN      — Twilio auth token\n  TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER     — Twilio sender number\n  ALLOWED_ORIGINS        — comma-separated CORS origins (default: *)\n\nNote: In non-production (NODE_ENV != 'production') the OTP is returned\nin the response body for easier testing — no SMS is sent.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "sg-sprint-2-2026-06-24"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl",      "value": "http://localhost:5000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "riderToken",   "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "driverToken",  "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminToken",   "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "testPhone",    "value": "+97798XXXXXXXX", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Sprint 2 — OTP Auth Flow",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP",
          "event": [{
            "listen": "test",
            "script": {
              "exec": [
                "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                "const r = pm.response.json();",
                "pm.test('Has OTP in dev mode', () => pm.expect(r.data).to.have.property('otp'));",
                "if (r.data?.otp) pm.collectionVariables.set('testOtp', r.data.otp);"
              ],
              "type": "text/javascript"
            }
          }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{testPhone}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "send-otp"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP — new user (expect 201)",
          "event": [{
            "listen": "test",
            "script": {
              "exec": [
                "pm.test('Status 201 or 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                "const r = pm.response.json();",
                "pm.test('Has accessToken', () => pm.expect(r.data).to.have.property('accessToken'));",
                "pm.test('Has refreshToken', () => pm.expect(r.data).to.have.property('refreshToken'));",
                "if (r.data?.accessToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('riderToken', 'Bearer ' + r.data.accessToken);",
                "if (r.data?.refreshToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', r.data.refreshToken);"
              ],
              "type": "text/javascript"
            }
          }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{testPhone}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{testOtp}}\",\n  \"role\": \"rider\",\n  \"device_id\": \"postman-device-001\",\n  \"device_name\": \"Postman Test\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "verify-otp"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Send OTP again (for resend test)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{testPhone}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "send-otp"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend OTP",
          "event": [{
            "listen": "test",
            "script": {
              "exec": [
                "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                "const r = pm.response.json();",
                "if (r.data?.otp) pm.collectionVariables.set('testOtp', r.data.otp);"
              ],
              "type": "text/javascript"
            }
          }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{testPhone}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/resend-otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "resend-otp"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP — wrong OTP (expect 400 INVALID_OTP)",
          "event": [{
            "listen": "test",
            "script": {
              "exec": [
                "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                "pm.test('Message is INVALID_OTP', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.equal('INVALID_OTP'));"
              ],
              "type": "text/javascript"
            }
          }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{testPhone}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"000000\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "verify-otp"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Send OTP — bad phone format (expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)",
          "event": [{
            "listen": "test",
            "script": {
              "exec": [
                "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                "pm.test('Validation error', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.equal('VALIDATION_ERROR'));"
              ],
              "type": "text/javascript"
            }
          }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"9800000000\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "send-otp"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Sprint 2 — Token Refresh & Rotation",
      "item": [
